# Secrets. The glob matters as much as the bare name: a plain `.env` rule
# leaves backups like `.env.bak-1785181407` untracked-but-committable, so one
# `git add -A` would publish ANTHROPIC_API_KEY to a public repo.
.env
.env.*
*.env
# ...but .env.example holds no secrets and documents the required vars, so it
# stays tracked. Without this it would be re-ignored if ever removed and re-added.
!.env.example
node_modules/

# Local runtime logs
server.out.log
server.err.log
*.log

# Raw per-target reports from run-eval.js (the committed summary lives in docs/evals/)
eval-runs/

# Local Claude Code settings
.claude/*
# ...except skills, which are project knowledge rather than local config
!.claude/skills/

# Captured leads and broker comp submissions (contact info) — never commit
leads.jsonl
comp-submissions.jsonl

# The team's internal contact book (names, phones, emails) — never commit
contacts.json

# Account store (emails + password hashes; * covers .tmp/.corrupt sidecars) — never commit
account-store.json*

# File fallbacks used only when Supabase isn't configured
search-cache.json
shared-reports.json
analytics.jsonl
market-pages-dynamic.json
comp-corpus.jsonl
dev-ideas.json
devlog-overrides.json
subject-sizes.json
guest-quota.jsonl

# Owner's local planning spreadsheets — not app code. Also covers the generated
# CompNinja-Ledger.xlsx and CompNinja-Profit-and-Loss.xlsx, which hold cost and
# revenue figures and, with a live Stripe key, customer payment descriptions.
# The ledger's inputs are ignored too — see the ledger DATA rule below.
CompNinja*.xlsx

# Ledger DATA — the company's actual finances. This repo is PUBLIC, and these
# files carry monthly costs, the LLC fee, and (now that Stripe is live) revenue
# and customer payment descriptions. The tooling and the *.example.csv templates
# are tracked; the real books are not. Same split as .env / .env.example above.
ledger/manual-entries.csv
ledger/recurring.csv
compninja-ai-costs.csv

# macOS Finder metadata. Committed once by accident on 2026-08-06 in the
# PR #40 merge; ignored so it cannot happen again.
.DS_Store

# Playwright MCP scratch output (page snapshots, console logs, screenshots).
# The browser tooling writes it into the repo root on every run, so it sat
# there untracked and growing. This checkout is shared by several sessions and
# its first rule is never to `git add -A`; an untracked pile in the root is a
# standing invitation to break that rule exactly once.
.playwright-mcp/

# SDD scratch: ledgers, briefs, review packages. Recreated per run.
.superpowers/

# Report-first outreach output. Drafts are unsent messages about real people's
# buildings, and outreach-seen.json is the list of who has already been
# written to — both are working state, not source.
outreach-drafts.md
outreach-seen.json
